        "api-server-processes",
        "stream-interval"
      ],
      "must_not_propose": [
        "speculative-mtp"
      ],
      "must_not_use_args": [
        "ngram",
        "--enforce-eager"
      ],
      "expected_skipped": [
        "cuda-graphs"
      ],
      "categories": [
        "host_bound"
      ],
      "why": "Requests waited while SMs had resident work on only 31% of cycles: the CPU side is not keeping the GPU fed. More API server processes take tokenization and HTTP handling off the engine's path, and streaming tokens in small groups cuts per-token work there. Both keep async scheduling and CUDA graphs on. vLLM already captures CUDA graphs by default, so no graph setup is added for a built-in runtime."
    },
